   148	    - Group the legend singletons by color and pair each color's two diagonal endpoints.
   149	    - Expand each paired endpoint box into all lattice cells inside that rectangle.
   150	    - Use the existing large blocks to infer the block scale and translation from legend-lattice cells to block positions.
   151	    - Paint the missing square blocks for every cell covered by every legend rectangle.
   152	
   153	    Key insight: The legend no longer lists target cells explicitly; each color contributes only two corner markers, and the hidden rectangle between them must be reconstructed before projecting it into the main block lattice.
